     There are no plans to make this stuff more complicated.  That
doesn't mean that you couldn't modify it yourself.  I don't remember
what problem started this thread.  If it's that the little animation
used to indicate resistance to magic attacks is too irritating,
then you may want to try toggling the `sparkle' option off instead
of trying to tweak its timing.  That won't affect missile traversal
display though (and I now have a vague recollection that missiles
were what started this afterall...).

     There's also the `null' option; toggling it may or may not
matter.  I don't know how nethack handles the termcap delay code for
OS/2.  There might be something to tweak there rather than trying to
switch from character I/O based delay to timer based delay.  But if
the timer code is now working, that hardcoded value (1/20th second
per use, IIRC) is the amount used on all platforms.


